==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}}, from {{etyl|xno|en}} {{m|fro|motteley||parti-colored}}, late 14th c., from {{der|en|ang|mot||speck}}, cognate with {{m|en|mote}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Comprising greatly [[varied]] [[element]]s, to the point of [[incongruity]]; [[heterogeneous]].
#* {{RQ:EHough PrqsPrc|II|0147}}
#*: Carried somehow, somewhither, for some reason, on these surging floods, were these travelers,{{nb...}}. Even such a boat as the ''Mount Vernon'' offered a total deck space so cramped as to leave secrecy or privacy well out of the question, even had the '''motley''' and democratic assemblage of passengers been disposed to accord either.
# Having many [[colour]]s; [[variegated]].

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|comprising greatly varied elements}} {{l|en|diverse}}, {{l|en|manifold}}; See also [[Thesaurus:heterogeneous]]
* {{sense|having many colours}} {{l|en|colorful}}, {{l|en|prismatic}}, {{l|en|variegated}}

